      "html": "<div class=\"story-inner\"><p class=\"story-eyebrow\">What it costs beside the others</p><h2 class=\"story-h2\">You are paying for licences nobody opens.</h2><p class=\"story-text\">Inspection apps bill per seat. Every person on the licence, every month, whether they inspect daily or have never opened it. Add the office, the relief staff and the people who do one check a year, and you are paying for all of them. Quickler charges for a phone number only when it did at least one check that month. Everyone else is free, so you add the whole team without thinking about it.</p><div class=\"story-article-body\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>Your team</th><th>Who inspects</th><th>Quickler</th><th>A per-seat app</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>10 people</td><td>2 regularly</td><td><strong>&pound;150</strong></td><td>&pound;190 to &pound;240</td></tr>\n<tr><td>20 people</td><td>5 regularly</td><td><strong>&pound;375</strong></td><td>&pound;380 to &pound;480</td></tr>\n<tr><td>30 people</td><td>5 regularly</td><td><strong>&pound;375</strong></td><td>&pound;570 to &pound;720</td></tr>\n<tr><td>50 people</td><td>6 regularly</td><td><strong>&pound;450</strong></td><td>&pound;950 to &pound;1,200</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Per-seat figures use the &pound;19 to &pound;24 a seat that the better-known inspection apps publish. Every price a month.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Being straight about it: if nearly everyone on your team inspects most days, for example five people all doing daily checks, a per-seat app will be cheaper than us. We are built for the firm where the whole team needs access and a handful actually do the walking.</p></div>"
